// FIXTURE 3 — THE NEGATIVE CASE. This one MUST keep warning after the
// exemption lands. Reduced from one of the 25 correct check_hand_placed_labels
// hits in the source deck.
//
// The shape is a card: a title plus two detail lines at a smaller size and a
// different colour, each its own text element constrained inside a visible,
// filled, stroked box. This is genuinely hand-placed text that belongs in a
// label: — the rule is right to complain, and the markup on main expresses it
// losslessly:
//
//   rect card [width: 290, height: 92, fill: background-light,
//              stroke: foreground-2, stroke_width: 2,
//              label: "Title<br><small><span fill=secondary-dark>first detail
//                      line</span></small><br><small><span fill=secondary-dark>
//                      second detail line</span></small>"]
//
// Expected on 8277305 AND after: label: texts "card_name", "card_one",
// "card_two" sit inside "card". If this goes quiet, the exemption is too broad
// — the box paints a fill AND a stroke and is nobody's sizing rect.

rect card [width: 290, height: 92, fill: background-light, stroke: foreground-2, stroke_width: 2]
constrain card.left = 30
constrain card.top = 20

text "Title" card_name [font_size: 15, fill: text-1]
constrain card_name.center_x = card.center_x
constrain card_name.top = card.top + 10

text "first detail line" card_one [font_size: 11, fill: secondary-dark]
constrain card_one.center_x = card.center_x
constrain card_one.top = card_name.bottom + 8

text "second detail line" card_two [font_size: 11, fill: secondary-dark]
constrain card_two.center_x = card.center_x
constrain card_two.top = card_one.bottom + 6
